    "body": "## Purpose\n\nWith dense (independent) data parallelism, every DFlash/DSpark drafter on a node shares one torch.compile cache directory, so a cached restart loads artifacts compiled on another replica's GPU and crashes (`CUDA driver error: invalid argument` in the draft's compiled graph).\n\nThe draft parallel config is built with `replace(parallel_config, ...)`, which re-derives the `init=False` field `data_parallel_index` from `data_parallel_rank` (0 on independent DP ranks). Fix: copy the target's `data_parallel_index` into the DFlash and DSpark draft parallel configs. (Keeping the field across `replace` in `ParallelConfig` itself would be a broader alternative.)\n\n## Test Plan\n\n`pytest tests/v1/worker/test_dspark_utils.py`. E2E on H200: `vllm serve Qwen/Qwen3-4B --data-parallel-size 2` with `RedHatAI/Qwen3-4B-speculator.dspark`, cold then cached start: main writes only `rank_0_0/dspark_head` and the cached start crashes; with this change both replicas get their own draft cache dir and both starts serve.\n\nAI assistance (Claude) was used; all changes were reviewed by the submitter.\n",
